{{Culture of Balisca}}
'''Avante!''' ({{literal translation|Forward!}}) is a [[w:Decentralization|decentralized]] {{W|anarchist}} {{W|collective}} of autonomous [[w:Clandestine cell system|cells]] originating in [[Balisca]]. Avante! emerged in the early-1990s following the [[Soviet Reformation]], initially as a hardcore [[W:Zine|zine]] that began operating as a collective in 1996. It has since published widely read articles and zines for the anarchist movement and distributed posters and books of its own publication.

Avante! cells have published books, released records, and organized national campaigns against [[W:Anti-globalization|globalization]] and [[W:Representative democracy|representative democracy]] in favor of radical community organizing. Less public splinter groups have carried out direct action (including arson and [[W:Hacktivism|hacktivism]]), hosted international conventions and other events, maintained local chapters, sparked riots, and toured with multimedia performance art or hardcore [[W:Anarcho-punk|anarcho-punk]] musical ensembles. The collective has received confederal media and academic attention, as well as criticism and praise from other anarchists for its activities and philosophy. 

Avante! has an association with [[Toju|/toju]], the ''[[Desconexión]]'' movement, and the wider Latin American anarcho-punk scene due to its relationship with artists in the genre and its publishing of ''Inside Front'' as well as more recently the contemporary [[W:anti-capitalism|anti-capitalist]] movement. 

